WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.660
See that ladder over there? That ladder motivated me to make this video because

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.680
no one should have to go through what I did to find it.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.060
'Cause breaking the bridge doesn't work,

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.860
finding your one character with the Cat Ring to survive the fall doesn't work

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:24.640
but what does work is killing this crawling tree.
Once it's dead, you'll hear an audio cue which signifies

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.100
a ladder has spawned...

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.680
And it's easy to miss it because who would think to go back up here?

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:39.980
At the top of Laddersmith Gilligan's wet dream is a Titanite Slab, one of the three in the DLC.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.640
Another place that looks out of reach is the colosseum structure

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.580
which looks an awful lot like the place we fought Priscilla in Dark Souls 1.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:55.180
It's accessed after breaking an illusory wall in the lower part of the cave with the flies.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:01.920
Once you navigate the roots down, you get led to an invasion by Livid Pyromancer Dunnel,

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:07.380
provided you've used an ember and apparently every painted world has its pyromancer

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.940
because the corpse you get the Parting Flame from

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.060
is also the same one that gives you Jeremiah's Robes in Dark Souls 1.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:20.860
It reads: "When Dunnel lost his hideous spouse, he gave his own pyromancy flame as an offering,

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:26.700
which transformed into a parting flame. Not long after, Dunnel became a mad spirit,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.820
damned to wander the lands."

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:34.100
Once you're done fighting Pyromancer Dunnel, just plunge down from the plank and hurry home.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.100
Don't worry, it's totally safe.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.580
The Parting Flame has a really interesting weapon art.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:44.580
You release your store of death echoes to gain a modest dose of Estus

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.760
...or not.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.840
So to get this to trigger, you need to keep it in an active equip slot

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.860
then build enough death echoes for you to cast it.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.880
So this translates to killing about twelve enemies for one charge of Estus at a time.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:05.900
Let's talk dialogue. This stuff is really interesting because the DLC adds a new way to trigger dialogue.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:11.940
You just have to return to a place or character for the second time after reloading the level.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:14.780
This is one example, the worst example.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.580
It's a seemingly pointless event where you get to here from the Corvian down in his cave.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:27.860
Corvian: "My very own home, now... (shuddering breath)

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.780
Vaati: Far more interesting is this piece of dialogue that triggers

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:37.380
the second time you approach the white haired woman after you've let her out of the archive attic.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.700
Painting Woman: "Those who aren't ken to fire cannot paint a world.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:48.600
Those absorbed by fire, must not paint a world.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.080
Don't worry, I haven't forgotten, Mother..."

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.340
Vaati: So, I'd say she fits the first line, right?

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:03.000
She's someone who isn't ken to fire and cannot yet paint a world.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:10.720
Ariandel who's the restorer of the Painted World, he fits the second line as he's absorbed by fire and,

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.420
perhaps, shouldn't have painted the world?

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:20.380
And as for the third line, it's trying to get us to ask a question: who is the white haired girl's mother?

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:25.200
Is it the woman depicted in the statues, holding the small girl, perhaps?

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:27.140
Or is it Priscilla?

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:33.200
We'll talk about that a bit later. Maybe the mother is related to the girl's Uncle Gael, as well.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.260
This man who prays to the...

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:40.100
Gael: "...merciful goddess, mother of the Forlorn..."

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.980
Vaati: But time will tell more about this character, hopefully.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:47.660
Especially considering how much of a tease her final piece of dialogue is.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:52.380
This triggers the second time you talk to her after killing the boss.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.420
Painting Woman: "My thanks, Ashen One.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.740
I can almost see the flame.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.920
Soon uncle Gael will bring me the pigment.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.980
I wonder if he has found it?

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.440
The dark soul of man..."

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:13.740
Vaati: It's almost like Gael is still out there and that he's looking for the dark soul of man,

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:20.800
the girl wishes to paint upon her canvas. So we'll have to go more into what this means in the lore video.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:26.180
But before we go, I just wanna say: do you think 'pigment' is a play on words for 'pygmy'?

00:04:26.420 --> 00:04:33.520
The Furtive Pygmy was the one who found the Dark Soul which split into humanity, after all.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.460
Maybe I'm looking too far, though.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:42.960
Number Eight. The crow-like Corvian also has final dialogue after you set fire to the Painting.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.820
Corvian: Ohhh, my, thank you.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.900
I can hear the crackling from here.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:56.780
The sound of my home, the painting of Ariandel, burning away...

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:04.340
When the world rots, we set it afire. For the sake of the next world.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:14.980
It's the one thing we do right, unlike those fools on the outside. (laughing)"

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:21.580
Vaati: So this tells us of the cyclical nature of the painting. This world that mirrors the outside, in a way.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.360
You also get a slab for your efforts here.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:28.920
So because the game was updated, my camera mods don't really work well right now

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:33.400
so it's hard to get close up to some of these models but it's worth talking about,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.520
what some things look like close up.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:40.220
They give us clues that we couldn't glean from just dialogue and descriptions.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.420
So this white haired girl is the best example.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:49.660
I might start calling her 'Aria', not the white haired girl and I call her Aria because

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:57.740
the painters so far have been Ariamis and Ariandel so, presumably, her name would take after theirs as well.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.800
'White haired girl' is just getting so annoying to say so.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:06.480
Aria. She has scales visible on her ankles and her neck

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:12.220
and also her eyes are a dark red and slitted like a reptiles'.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:20.360
Priscilla of Ariamis shares these same sort of scales and the same sort of eyes, though hers are green.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.640
So considering this dialogue:

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.200
Aria: "...I haven't forgotten, Mother..."

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:30.660
Vaati: It might be that Aria's mother is Priscilla given the similar scales and the eyes and the hair.

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:36.520
So Priscilla's definitely a promising candidate but we'll talk more about this in her lore video.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:42.880
So next, let's talk about the environment in a bit of detail just like we did the models.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:49.600
So, in particular, I wanna talk about three things. There's the snake statue at the end of the boss chamber,

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:55.780
there's the glass murals on the sides of Ariandel's chamber before he destroys them

00:06:55.780 --> 00:07:00.400
and there's the intertwined serpents upon the door of the church.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:05.140
But first let's talk about the snake statue because you come face to face with this thing

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:11.360
immediately after the boss fight and it's so deliberately placed and designed that

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:16.620
they want you to ask questions about this thing. Your attention is inevitably drawn towards it.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:25.760
So it's a statue because the face is textured like wood and the scales on the tail are torn and

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:31.280
maybe rotting away, revealing that it's actually cloth because you can see the thread between them.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:37.060
And since this cloth, these scales, are rotting away, you can actually see inside the tail which

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:41.860
reveals that it's actually metal or wood segments - cylindrical segments -

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.720
held together by wiring of some sort.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:52.500
And I call it a tail but really, it's more like her lower half. Hell, it's more like her entire body.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:58.600
Her torso is scaled like the tail is and it's not really like a hood because

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:04.620
if the head piece hadn't worn away at the front, we'd be calling this thing a snake, straight up.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.940
We wouldn't be calling it a human. It would be entirely covered.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:14.980
The shawl around this thing's shoulders is like fur and it reminds me of Priscilla's fur.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.340
So what is this thing and what does it represent?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:23.960
I don't know. I don't think anyone can really claim to know for sure but

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:31.380
I think it could be a representation of Priscilla but that's a stretch and I think it also could be someone else entirely.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:38.480
And I got a lot of tweets about this statue but I didn't get a single one about the glass murals on the panels

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:42.960
during phase one of the boss fight.
Look at this, it's creepy.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:49.340
Two dark womanly figures lean over a valley between two darkly wooded cliffs.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.620
One of these women is resting upon a sword or a staff

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:57.840
and the other one is reaching down to grasp a broken white chord.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.860
At the bottom, below, are the barely visible figures

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.520
of people reaching up towards them like a lot of hollows do in the game when they pray.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:14.360
Why is no one talking about this? If I had to guess, I would say that maybe they're the two other sisters

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:18.280
of the Sable Church of Londor, Elfriede being the third.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:23.940
The broken link could represent how the sisters are seeking to usurp the linking of the fire

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:27.640
and the figures at the bottom could be hollows worshiping them.

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:31.020
That's the best theory I got but what are your thoughts?

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:39.060
Lastly, engraved upon the door of the church are two snakes entwined. It reminds me of Kaathe and Frampt.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:43.100
Kaathe and Frampt represent two sides of a cycle.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:48.980
One light, one dark but both irreversibly intertwined and doomed to repeat.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:55.460
So I'd say that's what it's meant to represent but I don't know why it's here in the Painted World.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.940
But that's enough lore talk, let's talk about something very insignificant which is the crabs.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:05.940
I killed them so you don't have to. One drops a Crystal Gem. Wow.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:10.060
Number twelve. The wolf you fight on the way through the snow fields.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:13.280
So in case you ran past him and didn't kill him,

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:18.480
the wolf gives titanite if you defeat him in the snow field in both spots.

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:25.860
Number  thirteen, very interesting. If you chose the Lord of Hollows path and ending in the base game

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:32.900
then Friede and Vilhelm, formerly of the Sable Church which is related to that ending, have heard of you

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:37.840
and when you talk to them, they beseech you to return to your subjects,

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:42.000
to your hollows, instead of remaining in their Painted World.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:46.920
Friede: "Thou'rt the Lord of Londor, and have thine own subjects to guide."

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.700
Vaati: Yuria has something new to say as well.

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:53.180
Yuria: "Thy scent seemeth most familiar.

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:57.800
A sweet fragrance, long faded from our own bosoms.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:03.220
My lord, how this came to pass I know not, but...

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:09.720
Take heed. Kindness can wear upon one's principles..."

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.520
Vaati: And she has more dialogue when you kill Elfriede.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.920
Yuria: "Twas the soul of my sister.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:24.500
Elfriede... A poor wench turned to Ash, who would abandon Londor...

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:29.600
If thou wouldst, let it nourish thy Lordship.

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:34.260
And in return, do her one small kindness.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:41.560
Remember those who stayed by her to the end, in the shadows cast by fire...

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:48.720
And lastly, my Lord, take up thy rightful mantle, of usurper."

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:56.680
So for number fourteen, a couple of people on Reddit have pointed out a nice detail about the name 'Elfriede'

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:03.340
and the change of the name to 'Friede'. So, as we know, Elfriede was a member of the Sable Church

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:07.300
and both Yuria and Vilhelm refer to her by that name.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:12.880
But she renounced her past life and she found a new purpose in the painting.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:20.120
And here, in item descriptions and dialogue, she's known as Sister Friede without the 'El' at the start.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:26.420
And both of these names have meanings that line up with who she was at each time in her life.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:33.580
So 'Elfriede', according to Wikipedia, means 'elf strength' and when she had that name, it's at a point where

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:39.740
strength was a much bigger part in her life. The three sisters of the Sable Church were known as

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:43.980
very able swordmasters and they were known to be strong enough

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:47.100
to found the Church just between the three of them.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:51.680
So 'Elfriede' means strength and 'Friede', however,

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.940
is derived from a Germanic element 'frid' which means peace.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:13:04.560
And in the Painted World, described as a peaceful land, it makes sense that she would change her name to Friede.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:11.720
For she found a people to care for and even attempts to calmly reason with you to leave the painting.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:16.600
She doesn't want to fight but she knows she'll have to to keep the peace.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.780
So From's naming was really on point with this character.

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:27.680
And finally for number fifteen: don't kill any NPC in the Painted World. It's really not worth it this time around.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.040
You don't get any exciting weapons or anything like that.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:35.720
Vilhelm and Friede disappear, the crow-like Corvian drops nothing,

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:41.360
Aria cannot die for she says she has a world to paint and Gael...

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:49.520
Killing Gael, I think, locked my Soul Level 135 character out of the Painted World forever because

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:55.600
I can't get him to appear. I guess I'll have to take this character to new game plus now which kinda sucks...

00:13:56.040 --> 00:14:00.720
So thanks for watching guys. Hope you enjoy the Ariandel content to come and

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:04.700
let me know if there's something I missed down in the comments and go down in the comments and

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.580
see if there's anything cool down there that people have posted about.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.860
But thank you for watching and I'll see you next time.

